--- A function called with a list of ints and with a list of records is
--- two functions, a copy per kind (spec, Specialization): an int is a
--- record's none only where it is handed alone, a record or the 0 that
--- writes none. Joined, the copy's list of records or none had taken the
--- list of ints unconverted, an internal error in both modes (Rosetta
--- Code, Monads/List monad).
struct Pick [x, y]

fn firsts[xs]
    return xs[0]

ints = push[push[[], 1], 2]
log[firsts[ints]]
picks = push[[], Pick[1, 2]]
log[firsts[picks].y]
zeros_too = push[push[[], 0], 0]
log[type[firsts[zeros_too]]]
